{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00583",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.51,
      "end_seconds": 10.6,
      "duration_seconds": 10.09,
      "text": "So, um, I had the ultrasound last month, and the report said something about my liver. I wasn't sure what to..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 12.13,
      "end_seconds": 21.6,
      "duration_seconds": 9.47,
      "text": "Okay, take your time. Let's start with what the report said. Do you have it with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 23.01,
      "end_seconds": 31.5,
      "duration_seconds": 8.49,
      "text": "Right here. It says, uh, fatty liver. Mild. And I've been kind of freaking out since."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 34.34,
      "end_seconds": 47.84,
      "duration_seconds": 13.5,
      "text": "I understand. Fat in the liver is quite common, and mild is the reassuring word there. Your family doctor sent you to talk through your medicines, right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 49.54,
      "end_seconds": 58.28,
      "duration_seconds": 8.74,
      "text": "Yeah. She said the liver can be affected by, you know, tablets. So I brought the list."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 59.61,
      "end_seconds": 67.97,
      "duration_seconds": 8.36,
      "text": "Good thinking. We'll go through each. First, how have you been feeling? Any symptoms?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 70.41,
      "end_seconds": 81.02,
      "duration_seconds": 10.61,
      "text": "Not much. Some mild discomfort on my right side, under the ribs. Sometimes. It's, um, more of a nagging than a pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.1,
      "end_seconds": 87.8,
      "duration_seconds": 4.7,
      "text": "A nagging discomfort under the right ribs. How often?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.51,
      "end_seconds": 96.64,
      "duration_seconds": 7.13,
      "text": "A couple of times a week? After big meals, I guess. I haven't really..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 97.91,
      "end_seconds": 102.77,
      "duration_seconds": 4.86,
      "text": "That's okay. You haven't noticed it anywhere else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 103.52,
      "end_seconds": 106.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "No. Just there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.92,
      "end_seconds": 114.03,
      "duration_seconds": 5.11,
      "text": "Have you noticed your eyes or skin looking yellow?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 116.97,
      "end_seconds": 124.72,
      "duration_seconds": 7.75,
      "text": "No, no yellow. My wife would have said something, she notices everything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 127.36,
      "end_seconds": 133.51,
      "duration_seconds": 6.15,
      "text": "Good. Now the medicines. What's the first one on your list?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 136.41,
      "end_seconds": 142.68,
      "duration_seconds": 6.27,
      "text": "Metformin. 500 mg, twice a day, with meals. For my diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 145.53,
      "end_seconds": 152.65,
      "duration_seconds": 7.12,
      "text": "Metformin, 500 mg twice a day, for the diabetes. Which type of diabetes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 153.76,
      "end_seconds": 158.57,
      "duration_seconds": 4.81,
      "text": "Type 2. Diagnosed about six years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.55,
      "end_seconds": 163.26,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "Thanks. Next?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 164.09,
      "end_seconds": 173.52,
      "duration_seconds": 9.43,
      "text": "Atorvastatin. 20 mg, at bedtime. It's for, uh, cholesterol. I've had high cholesterol for a long time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.28,
      "end_seconds": 184.06,
      "duration_seconds": 7.78,
      "text": "Atorvastatin, 20 mg at bedtime, for your cholesterol. Any muscle aches with that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.98,
      "end_seconds": 195.2,
      "duration_seconds": 8.22,
      "text": "I don't think so. Hmm, maybe my calves sometimes, but I don't know if that's the..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 196.9,
      "end_seconds": 202.22,
      "duration_seconds": 5.32,
      "text": "We'll keep an eye on that. What else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 203.24,
      "end_seconds": 210.08,
      "duration_seconds": 6.84,
      "text": "Lisinopril, 10 mg. Once a day, in the morning. For blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.98,
      "end_seconds": 217.06,
      "duration_seconds": 6.08,
      "text": "Lisinopril, 10 mg once a day for blood pressure. Is that all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 220.05,
      "end_seconds": 231.48,
      "duration_seconds": 11.43,
      "text": "Oh, and the baby aspirin. 81 mg. My cardiologist, um, a few years ago... Anyway, I take it every morning too."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.09,
      "end_seconds": 241.41,
      "duration_seconds": 8.32,
      "text": "Aspirin, 81 mg every morning. So four medicines in total. Anything over the counter? Supplements?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 244.41,
      "end_seconds": 251.88,
      "duration_seconds": 7.47,
      "text": "Nothing else. I'm kind of scared to take anything extra now, because of the liver."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.42,
      "end_seconds": 259.97,
      "duration_seconds": 6.55,
      "text": "That's sensible. Just check with us or the pharmacist before you add anything new."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 261.27,
      "end_seconds": 263.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 265.69,
      "end_seconds": 273.54,
      "duration_seconds": 7.85,
      "text": "Is there anything in the family I should know about? Liver trouble, or other illness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 275.08,
      "end_seconds": 281.27,
      "duration_seconds": 6.19,
      "text": "My father had diabetes too. He had it for a long time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.78,
      "end_seconds": 297.25,
      "duration_seconds": 6.47,
      "text": "Okay, thank you. Let me have a quick feel of your tummy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 305.82,
      "end_seconds": 314.82,
      "duration_seconds": 9.0,
      "text": "Your abdomen is soft, and I can't feel anything unusual under the ribs on the right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 316.11,
      "end_seconds": 322.06,
      "duration_seconds": 5.95,
      "text": "That's a relief. I was afraid you'd find a lump or something."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 324.73,
      "end_seconds": 337.13,
      "duration_seconds": 12.4,
      "text": "Not at all. Let me also read your numbers. Blood pressure is 134 over 82, and weight is 94 kilograms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 339.38,
      "end_seconds": 344.42,
      "duration_seconds": 5.04,
      "text": "The weight's gone up a little. I know. I'm, um..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 345.44,
      "end_seconds": 361.06,
      "duration_seconds": 15.62,
      "text": "It happens. Let me say back what I'm hearing. Mild fatty liver on the scan, a nagging right-sided discomfort now and then, and four regular medicines."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 361.87,
      "end_seconds": 364.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "Yes, that's it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 367.32,
      "end_seconds": 381.82,
      "duration_seconds": 14.5,
      "text": "Those four medicines are all well-established, and none is a common cause of fatty liver. I'd like to order liver blood tests to see how your liver is working."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 383.43,
      "end_seconds": 386.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "Okay. Like, regular blood work?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 387.6,
      "end_seconds": 396.3,
      "duration_seconds": 8.7,
      "text": "Yes, a simple blood draw. You can do it at the lab on your way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 397.87,
      "end_seconds": 405.82,
      "duration_seconds": 7.95,
      "text": "And what should I do about the fat? Is there a pill for it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 406.97,
      "end_seconds": 419.87,
      "duration_seconds": 12.9,
      "text": "Not really. Gradual weight loss, regular movement, and cutting back on sugary drinks help the most. Even a small loss makes a difference."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 422.79,
      "end_seconds": 430.44,
      "duration_seconds": 7.65,
      "text": "I can try that. I just... I'm not sure where to start."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 433.01,
      "end_seconds": 442.66,
      "duration_seconds": 9.65,
      "text": "Start small. Swap one sugary drink a day for water, and add a ten-minute walk after dinner."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 443.71,
      "end_seconds": 448.53,
      "duration_seconds": 4.82,
      "text": "Okay. Water and a walk. I can do that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 450.32,
      "end_seconds": 462.03,
      "duration_seconds": 11.71,
      "text": "Exactly. I'd like to see you again in three months, so we can look at the blood results and how things are going."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 462.93,
      "end_seconds": 468.65,
      "duration_seconds": 5.72,
      "text": "Three months. Okay. Thank you. I feel a lot calmer now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 470.11,
      "end_seconds": 476.82,
      "duration_seconds": 6.71,
      "text": "You did well to come in, and bring the list. See you then."
    }
  ]
}
